# Implementation Plan - Sign-in Endpoint

This plan outlines the implementation of the sign-in flow (endpoint `/auth/signin`) for the authentication service. It mirrors the design patterns, repositories, and caching strategies established in the sign-up flow.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Membership Validation Decision:** 
> When a user signs in, we check if they have a `Membership` record for the specified `clientId` (App). If they do not, we will throw a `"Not a member of this application"` error. Alternatively, we could automatically create a membership for them if the app exists. We propose throwing an error to preserve strict access control.

> [!NOTE]
> **Failed Attempt Rate-Limiting:**
> For sign-in, we will implement rate-limiting that increments attempts specifically on **failed** authentication attempts (e.g. wrong password). This prevents locked-out scenarios for valid users logging in correctly on their first attempt, unlike sign-up where rate limits increment on every step 1 initiation.

